{
 "id": "spring-bracket-pacf",
 "brief": "A bracket that anchors my arm's counterbalance spring, carbon-fibre nylon (PA-CF) on an FDM\nprinter, printed with the plate face down (layers along +Z). It screws flat to the arm's side\nplate (z = 0) with three M4 screws along Z at (0, 0), (30, 0) and (15, 25), each through a\n4.5 mm hole in a 10 mm diameter, 4 mm thick boss (z = 0 to 4), with the heads on top needing\n8 mm diameter clearance above. The spring hooks into a 6 mm hole along X through an eye at\n(15, 8, 30) with 3 mm of wall round it. The part fits in x = -8 to 38, y = -8 to 33, z = 0 to 36.\nThe spring pulls the eye with up to 150 N along -Y, and it cycles every time the arm moves.\nSafety factor 2.5.",
